{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>That which you will bake, bake.</b> Rashi explained (Rashi on Exodus 16:23): Whatever you wish to bake in the oven or to boil in water — bake and boil it today for two days. If so, he should say: \"That which you will bake — from the double portion of the omer that is in your hands — bake today, and that which you will boil — from their double portion — boil now, and all the remainder left over for you from what you are satiated with today, set aside for yourselves to be kept until morning.\" And in the morning, when they saw that it had not become wormy, they came before him, for they did not wish to eat of it from day to day even though he had permitted them to set it aside until morning. And in the morning he permitted it to them: \"Eat it today only, for therefore I said to set it aside for safekeeping.\" And he informed them in the manner of a commandment that <b>today you will not find it in the field</b>, for HaShem will do so on account of it being a holy Sabbath to YHWH. And what he said, <b>and all the remainder</b> — it is possible that He did not give them a fixed measure in this, but rather they would eat as much as they desired on the sixth day, for the remainder would suffice for the Sabbath, for it is the blessing of HaShem.\n\nAnd Rabbi Abraham said (Ibn Ezra on Exodus 16:23): \"That which you will bake — according to your custom — bake for yourselves today,\" and this is the omer known to them. \"And all the remainder,\" which is the second omer, \"set aside for yourselves to be kept until morning,\" and he did not tell them what to do with it. And in the morning he said to them: \"Eat it today.\" If so, they would eat it on the Sabbath raw, without baking or boiling it on the eve of the Sabbath, and they would make cakes of it according to their custom. But the first interpretation is more correct, and so is the opinion of Onkelos (Targum Onkelos on Exodus 16:23)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "In the paraphrase of the predicted instruction, Ramban reconstructs the expected wording had the verse followed Rashi's logic; the Hebrew here is Ramban's own rearrangement, not a direct biblical quotation."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:09:30.418224727Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}